WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.820
A $16 billion Kenyan oil refinery breaks ground to boost East African industry, despite protests over land compensation from locals. This is Omni View, episode 192. Nigerian billionaire Aliko Dangote and Kenyan president William Ruto launched construction of the facility in Lamu on Kenyan's northern coast. The refinery is designed to process 700,000 barrels of crude oil per day once complete. It will become East Africa's

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:35.800
only refinery. Leaders from Uganda, Ethiopia, Togo, and Benin attended the event.

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:40.460
Regional governments have been offered a combined 30% stake in the project.

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:46.360
Dangote described the project as proof that African-led industrial development can succeed.

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:52.560
He pointed to his existing leaky refinery in Nigeria as evidence that the model works and can

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:58.980
be repeated. President Ruto framed the refinery as a declaration that Africa will process and add

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:02.960
value to its own resources rather than exporting raw materials.

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:10.180
Local campaign groups Save LAMU, represented by co-founder Walid Ali, raised concerns about

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:11.500
environmental impacts.

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:17.180
The group called for release of the full environmental impact assessment to review proposed mitigation

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:17.860
steps.

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:24.020
BBC reporting presented both the official optimism and the local demands for transparency

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:26.000
without endorsing either view.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:31.900
Project backers argue that the refinery will create long-term jobs and energy security

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:37.080
for multiple countries. They note the government has already limited land take to only what

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:41.000
is required and is offering compensation through established channels.

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:46.500
Opponents counter that past projects have overlooked environmental risks to coastal communities.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:52.180
They add that full assessment findings must be public before irreversible construction proceeds,

00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:55.560
seeds, noting that mitigation details remain unavailable.

00:01:56.060 --> 00:01:57.240
What happens next?

00:01:57.660 --> 00:02:02.500
The first phases of construction will test how the compensation and review process is unfold

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:03.160
on the ground.

00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:09.800
A fly Dubai co-pilot allegedly stabbed the captain on a flight carrying 174 passengers

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:11.680
and attempted to seize control.

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:17.740
The plane dropped more than 17,000 feet before passengers and crew regained the cockpit and

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:19.100
diverted to Saudi Arabia.

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:25.200
India. The injured captain, an Indian national, is in stable condition in hospital. Israeli

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:29.980
prime minister Benjamin Netanyahu said it is too early to determine any motive or

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:35.900
link to Iran. Netanyahu described the captain's actions as heroic and credited passengers

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:41.600
with preventing a larger disaster. Israel's defense minister labeled the incident an attempted

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:47.340
terror attack. US President Donald Trump told Fox News the attacker may have been acting

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:53.040
as a terrorist or for other reasons. The Indian Embassy confirmed the captain's stable condition.

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:57.060
Indian Prime Minister Narendra Modi praised his resistance.

00:02:57.960 --> 00:03:02.980
BBC and Reuters accounts both note that authorities have not yet released a confirmed motive.

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:07.440
Tennessee halted an execution after a second lethal injection failed.

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:13.320
Death row inmate Krista Pike survived the attempt at River Bend maximum security institution

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:16.060
after receiving two doses of pentobarbital.

00:03:16.660 --> 00:03:21.620
She was moved to hospital for life-saving measures while still breathing and with a detectable heartbeat.

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:25.420
Tennessee Governor Bill Lee ordered a third-party review

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:28.420
and canceled the state's remaining execution for the year.

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:32.500
Pike's legal team filed an emergency motion during the procedure,

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:37.400
arguing the protocol did not clearly address what happens after two failed injections.

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:41.420
The victim's mother told NBC News the process was a mess.

00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:45.740
The Tennessee Department of Corrections stated it stands by its actions.

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:49.520
The governor's review aims to establish exactly what occurred.

00:03:50.380 --> 00:03:55.800
BBC reporting notes this follows an earlier 2026 postponement in the same state due to

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:57.180
vain access difficulties.

00:03:57.980 --> 00:04:02.480
Russian forces conducted their heaviest combined assault on Ukraine's energy infrastructure

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:03.160
in months.

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:08.460
The strikes killed seven people and triggered emergency power cuts in Kiev and surrounding

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:08.900
regions.

00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:13.760
operations. Officials warned of a difficult winter ahead as heating and power systems face

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:19.220
repeated damage. Ukrainian authorities described the strikes as targeting civilian energy

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:24.900
supplies critical for winter survival. Russian statements have framed similar past operations

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:31.520
as strikes on military-related infrastructure. France 24 reporting loads the attack coincides

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:36.020
with broader concerns over Ukraine's ability to maintain power through the coming season.

00:04:36.020 --> 00:04:42.100
A model called Maxwell, developed by the Chinese Academy of Sciences Institute of Artificial

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:48.180
Intelligence for Industries, scored 91.9 on the MetaWorld benchmark for robot physical

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:48.700
tasks.

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:51.720
That is the highest result recorded so far.

00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:58.040
The benchmark, created by researchers from Stanford, UC Berkeley, and others, tests performance

00:04:58.040 --> 00:05:02.100
on 50 everyday actions such as grasping objects and opening drawers.

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:07.480
The result places Maxwell ahead of submissions from teams including physical intelligence,

00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:11.140
Google DeepMind, Alibaba, and Carnegie Mellon.

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:15.480
Second place went to a Shenzhen-based model with 90.0.

00:05:16.100 --> 00:05:21.120
South China Morning Post coverage highlights the score as evidence of rapid Chinese progress

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.860
in embodied AI systems.

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:26.700
India recorded its weakest rainfall since 2015.

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:31.820
The shortfall led to lower rice yields and higher input costs for farmers in northern

00:05:31.820 --> 00:05:32.380
states.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:37.780
Traders in markets such as Carnal report that weaker harvests typically reduce spending

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:41.660
on items from tractors to wetting goods in the months after the months soon.

00:05:42.420 --> 00:05:47.380
South China Morning Post reporting links the rainfall shortfall directly to expected pressure

00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:49.220
on consumption in rural areas.

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:54.920
Farmers describe needing extra fertilizer and chemicals to protect yields, increasing their

00:05:54.920 --> 00:06:00.600
costs at a time of lower output. Progress worth knowing comes from Hong Kong, where the

00:06:00.600 --> 00:06:05.360
health chief is moving to protect the nurse recruitment pipeline. Secretary for Health

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:11.020
Low-Chung Mao warned that exaggerated claims of nurse unemployment after graduation could

00:06:11.020 --> 00:06:16.520
discourage new entrance to the profession. He noted that training takes time and that inaccurate

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:22.480
statements risk reducing recruitment numbers the city will later need. Low stated the city

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:24.880
would bear the consequences if recruitment falls.

00:06:25.460 --> 00:06:27.260
He emphasized that nurse numbers

00:06:27.260 --> 00:06:28.980
cannot be increased overnight.

00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:31.280
The remarks followed public debate

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:32.720
over employment prospects.

00:06:33.560 --> 00:06:35.300
South China Morning Post coverage

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:37.160
presents the statement as an attempt

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:39.340
to safeguard future staffing levels.

00:06:39.780 --> 00:06:42.680
To really understand how large infrastructure projects

00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:45.140
secure land and manage local opposition,

00:06:45.640 --> 00:06:47.660
consider the sequence of steps that begins

00:06:47.660 --> 00:06:49.540
with government designation of land

00:06:49.540 --> 00:06:51.260
through eminent domain powers.

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:57.660
Officials then conduct impact assessments, whose findings set mitigation requirements and payment levels.

00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:05.680
Developers can accept only the portion needed, yet they still face organized campaigns that demand full public release of those studies.

00:07:06.420 --> 00:07:16.500
Historical parallels from earlier Nigerian and Kenyan projects show that when assessments remain partially confidential, trust erodes even if formal compensation occurs.

00:07:16.500 --> 00:07:21.200
Communities cannot verify where other promised protections will materialize.

00:07:21.680 --> 00:07:26.620
Knowing this mechanism lets readers distinguish between disputes rooted in process transparency,

00:07:27.360 --> 00:07:30.320
and those rooted in outright rejection of the project itself.

00:07:31.040 --> 00:07:35.500
When you next see claims that protests are merely games played by local marketers,

00:07:36.060 --> 00:07:39.280
check whether the environmental assessment has been published in full

00:07:39.280 --> 00:07:42.160
and what specific mitigation measures it lists.

00:07:42.160 --> 00:07:48.500
If you want to go deeper on the Kenyan refinery, compare how BBC World News and South China

00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:50.300
Morning Post are covering the story.

00:07:50.740 --> 00:07:55.300
Tomorrow, watch for whether regional governments accept any of the offered stakes in the

00:07:55.300 --> 00:07:56.080
Lamu project.

00:07:56.700 --> 00:07:57.640
That's Omnivu.

00:07:58.100 --> 00:08:03.800
As always, compare outlets, look for primary documents, and separate what's known from what's

00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:04.200
assumed.

